 "comment":"WP-2.4b. Three scenes on the stone platform. (1) Cart 0 runs at set_motion 1.0 along rails on a stone ledge (y = 62, x = -7..-2, z = -3) and off its end: off the rails (EntityMinecart.java:416-445) its motion is clamped to 0.4, halved on the ground, 0.95 in the air; it falls, hits the stone wall at x = 1 in the air (isCollidedHorizontally) and drops to the floor. (2) Carts 1 and 2 meet head-on on a track along x at z = 3: applyEntityCollision of two plain carts averages their motions and pushes them apart (:696-705), the dz = 0 of a shared track keeping the (dx * motionZ + dz * prevPosX)^2 test (:676-680) at 0. (3) Cart 3 runs along a track at z = -7 past cart 4, parked off the rails on the floor 0.7 to the side at x = 5.5: the moving cart's getCollisionBox(other) is the other's box (:45-47), so cart 4 blocks it physically, while the vanilla bug of the collision test (dz * prevPosX, about (0.7 * 4.5)^2 > 5) skips every cart-to-cart push between them. rng_state and entity_state every tick.",
